    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BLUF",
      "narration_text": "Throttling means DynamoDB rejects requests and asks you to retry, even when the table has room to spare. What matters is where the traffic lands.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "BrutalistHesitantWriter",
          "props": {
            "text": "A table with spare capacity won't throttle.\nWhere traffic lands decides.",
            "triggerWords": "won't throttle",
            "replacementWords": "can still throttle",
            "face": "serif",
            "fontSize": 64,
            "lineSpacing": 1.25,
            "align": "center",
            "seed": "dynamodb-hot-partition-b01",
            "ink": "#3D3929",
            "accent": "#D97757",
            "bg": "#F2F0E9"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T22:45:24.725321+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "writer types the claim"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.5,
            "event": "corrected to 'can still throttle'"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "lead_silence_s": 0.8,
      "actual_duration_s": 9.75
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "SETUP",
      "narration_text": "An event service writes thousands of records a second, all with one partition key, the field that decides placement: today's date. DynamoDB hashes it to pick a partition. Same key, same partition.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "AgentToolLoop",
          "props": {
            "stages": [
              "EVENTS",
              "KEY 2026-10-23",
              "HASH(KEY)",
              "ONE PARTITION"
            ],
            "executeIndex": 3,
            "loopBack": false,
            "ports": [],
            "sparkLine": "Same key, same partition."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T22:46:37.963039+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.05,
            "event": "events → key → hash → one partition, in narration order"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.7
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "LIMIT",
      "narration_text": "The table allows ten thousand writes a second, but each partition is capped at about a thousand write units, where one unit is one write up to a kilobyte. Adaptive capacity helps, but it cannot raise that cap.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "EvidenceBars",
          "props": {
            "title": "Write capacity: whole table vs one partition",
            "note": "1 write unit = one write per second, up to 1 KB",
            "bars": [
              {
                "label": "Whole table",
                "value": 10000,
                "display": "10,000 / s"
              },
              {
                "label": "One partition",
                "value": 1000,
                "display": "1,000 / s"
              }
            ],
            "accentIndex": 1,
            "caption": "Every write for today lands on the one partition",
            "sparkLine": "Spare capacity, wrong place."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-23T22:47:48.138316+00:00"
          }
        },
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.1,
            "event": "whole-table bar to 10,000"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.22,
            "event": "one-partition bar stops at 1,000 (accent)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.06
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "FIX",
      "narration_text": "The fix is a data-model change called write sharding: spread today's writes across ten keys, shard zero to shard nine. Ten keys, ten places to land.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "EvidenceBars",
          "props": {
            "title": "Writes per second per key",
